functor: 1
title: tall
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`tall` · deform · a taller version; the straight parts grow and the ends keep their shape.

# Form

`x.tall` on a symbol, `(a + b).tall` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `integral.tall` | $integral.tall$ | built and cached |
| `x.tall` | $x.tall$ | built and cached |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | A taller version; the straight parts grow and the ends keep their shape. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | Use a `sym` to give a recipe a short name. |
| Construction | A changed outline of the base. The straight parts grow and the ends and thin strokes keep their shape. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.
- Makes the base half again as tall. Stems and straight parts grow, the ends keep their shape.

# From LaTeX

`\bigl(` and the like, for a bigger glyph.

